WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.490
Drop the number five into a machine.

2
00:00:02.540 --> 00:00:05.270
It doubles your number, then adds three.

3
00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.890
Out comes thirteen.

4
00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:12.430
Now a second machine, completely empty,
has to turn thirteen back into five.

5
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:13.830
What goes inside?

6
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.130
Halve, then subtract three?

7
00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.970
Subtract three, then halve?

8
00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.780
Does the order even matter?

9
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.830
In this mission, you'll
use function notation.

10
00:00:22.880 --> 00:00:26.950
F of x equals three x minus
five means multiply by three,

11
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.850
then subtract five.

12
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:31.940
You'll put two functions together,
doing one after the other,

13
00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:33.980
to make a composite function.

14
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:38.840
And you'll find inverse functions:
functions that undo another function.

15
00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:41.870
Your mission: find the
machine that undoes it.
